--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0002-tags-on-posts.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+---
+type: adr
+status: stable
+entities: [Post, Tag, PostTag]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/PostResource.ts
+  - app/Http/Validators/PostValidator.ts
+  - db/schema.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-fable-5-1/1.0", at: 2026-09-29T17:14:49.326Z }
+---
+
+# Tags on posts
+
+## Context
+
+The posts list is one long feed, so readers cannot find posts on a topic.
+Authors need to tag posts, and topic pages and a tag cloud will later read
+the same data, so the table, prop and parameter names are a contract.
+
+## Decision
+
+- **Storage.** `tags (id, name unique)` and the pivot `post_tags (post_id,
+  tag_id)`, one row per tag attached to a post. Names are case-sensitive.
+- **Input.** The forms send one `tags` string of comma-separated names.
+  `parseTagNames()` trims each name, drops empty entries and collapses
+  duplicates; after that a post may have at most 5 tags of 1–30 characters
+  each, counted in code points. The rules sit in `PostPayloadSchema`, so a
+  violation is refused like any other invalid field, reported on `tags`.
+- **Saving.** `Post.syncTags()` makes the submitted names the post's exact
+  tag set inside the transaction that writes the post. A missing or empty
+  field means no tags. A tag no post uses any more stays in `tags`.
+- **Output.** `PostResource` always carries `tags: string[]`, the names
+  sorted alphabetically (`localeCompare` in `en`), `[]` without tags.
+- **Filtering.** `/posts?tag=<name>` lists the posts carrying the tag,
+  newest first, ten per page; the page links keep the filter. An unknown
+  tag is an empty list. A blank `tag` is treated as no filter.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Every query that feeds `PostResource` has to eager-load `tags`; a query
+  that does not reports `[]` instead of failing.
+- The filtered list pages over `post_tags`, so its cost does not grow with
+  the number of posts a tag carries.
+- Keyword search (`posts.search`) ignores the tag filter.
+- Unused tags accumulate; pruning them is left to a later change.
